# Hotel Munich Frontend Mobile - Environment Configuration
# =========================================================
# Copy this file to .env.local. For LOCAL DEVELOPMENT you can leave
# everything commented out — the app auto-detects the backend URL from
# the current hostname (see src/constants/keys.ts). The .env.local file
# only needs entries for the special cases below.
#
# Auto-detection works for:
#   - In-browser preview     localhost:3000 → backend on localhost:8000
#   - Real phone on Wi-Fi    192.168.x.y:3000 → backend on 192.168.x.y:8000
#   - Any other LAN IP       same hostname, port 8000
#
# You only need to set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL when:
#   (a) deploying to staging/prod where the API lives on a different
#       hostname than the UI (e.g. app.hotel.com + api.hotel.com), OR
#   (b) the backend is bound to a non-8000 port, OR
#   (c) you're testing against a remote API while the UI runs locally.
#
# Examples (uncomment + edit one):
#
# Staging VM (GCP):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://VM_IP:8000
#
# Production with split hostnames:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com
